    }
    /* A caption that names an artifact carries a long file path. It breaks
       inside the word rather than widening the page at 320px. */
    .fig figcaption code {
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }

    /* One plate grammar, three new plates (ADR-004, ADR-013). Page-scoped.

       COPY. The five text rules below are
       src/pages/projects/faithfulness-judge.astro at bd00680, from line 105,
       with the `fj-` prefix changed to `kb-`. The two plates above this page
       already carry the `rp-` and `hp-` prefixes, so nothing collides, and the
       two marker ids these plates add carry a digit for the same reason.

       All three new plates are monochrome. Oxide (--accent-warm) on this page
       marks the miss the eval exists to find and the default that was taken
       back, and both readings are recorded above. Nothing on these three plates
       is either one, so every state is a word plus a shape: a solid box against
       a dashed box, and a filled mark against an empty row.

       SVG text inherits from <body>, so every text class names its own font.
       Max-width 260 keeps one viewBox unit at one CSS pixel down to 320px. The
       plates sit inside .decision, which has no horizontal padding, so the
       measured container is the article track and not a narrower one. */
    .kb-plate {
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 260px;
      height: auto;
      margin: 4px 0 0;
    }
    .kb-plate .kb-lane {
      fill: var(--muted);
      font-family: var(--font);
      font-size: 10px;
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    }
    .kb-plate .kb-title {
      fill: var(--text);
      font-family: var(--font);
      font-size: 11px;
      font-weight: 500;
    }
    .kb-plate .kb-state {
