    /* kb1-ranks. Two ranked lists that agree on one file.

       NEITHER LIST IS PLACED AT ITS MEASURED RANK, and the caption says so. A
       hand-drawn plate that placed a row at its measured rank would publish
       that rank as a position, with no producer and no gate. The ranks stay in
       the caption, where a reader reads them.

       The dashed band is the stub the query asked for, and it is the state the
       page argues about. Solid against dashed is the shape and the words carry
       the rest, because Geist has no glyph for the symbols that would replace
       them (the .two-fail comment on false-green.astro records that). */
    .kb1-plate .kb1-box {
      fill: var(--bg);
      stroke: var(--rule-strong);
      stroke-width: 1;
    }
    .kb1-plate .kb1-agree {
      fill: var(--bg);
      stroke: var(--text);
      stroke-width: 1.5;
